1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
Autonomous AI coding agents can generate entire features in minutes,

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:12,000
but running them in production without strict tool sandboxing is an engineering disaster waiting to happen.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:19,000
On the SWE-bench benchmark of 2,294 real-world software issues,

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:26,000
baseline frontier models resolved under five percent of tasks, highlighting the challenge of repository-scale autonomous engineering.

5
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Research from MetaGPT shows that structuring agent collaboration with Standard Operating Procedures helps prevent circular coordination loops.

6
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Without boundary contracts, unconstrained agent runs risk mutating workspace state or triggering silent regression bugs.

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:48,000
The solution is deterministic runtime governance.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Tools must execute inside isolated sandboxes with strict schema contracts, structured error handling, and hardware-enforced boundaries.

9
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Comprehensive preflight verification and automated testing gates validate system state before changes deploy to live environments.

10
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Build verifiable tool boundaries first, and your autonomous agents will operate with measurable reliability.
